From: Avula Sri Charan <asrichar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Apr 2025 15:31:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: select WMI endpoints for QCN9274 AMSS mode

QCN9274 hw2 supports both single-PHY and split-PHY firmware.  The
upstream hardware parameters advertise the maximum of two radios, but
the single-PHY AMSS image provides only the primary WMI control service.
Using the maximum while booting that image makes ath12k request the
nonexistent WMI MAC1 service, which the firmware rejects with HTC status
1.  The driver then continues with a partially initialized control path.

Remember the AMSS mode selected from the QCN9274 OTP board ID and select
the single-PHY WMI mode before HTC is initialized when regular AMSS is in
use.  Keep the two-endpoint setup for boards that select amss_dualmac.

Based-on: 45b54d3221a7e1123a2282c8fd42b7819b01828d
Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/system/feeds/wlan-open/-/blob/1ee3a4ab7c59ceaff347c4668fc6c7604a04c323/patches/ath12k/0127-QSDK-PLATFORM-wifi-ath12k-Enable-amss_dualmac.bin-lo.patch
Signed-off-by: Avula Sri Charan <asrichar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h |  1 +
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c  |  2 ++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c  |  4 +++-
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
@@ -1186,6 +1186,7 @@ struct ath12k_base {
 		const u8 *amss_dualmac_data;
 		size_t amss_dualmac_len;
 		const u8 *m3_data;
+		bool dualmac;
 		size_t m3_len;
 
 		DECLARE_BITMAP(fw_features, ATH12K_FW_FEATURE_COUNT);
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -344,6 +344,8 @@ int ath12k_mhi_register(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci)
 		}
 	}
 
+	ab->fw.dualmac = dualmac;
+
 	if (dualmac) {
 		if (ab->fw.amss_dualmac_data && ab->fw.amss_dualmac_len > 0) {
 			/* use MHI firmware file from firmware-N.bin */
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -10144,7 +10144,9 @@ int ath12k_wmi_attach(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	ab->wmi_ab.preferred_hw_mode = WMI_HOST_HW_MODE_MAX;
 
 	/* It's overwritten when service_ext_ready is handled */
-	if (ab->hw_params->single_pdev_only)
+	if (ab->hw_params->single_pdev_only ||
+	    (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_QCN9274_HW20 &&
+	     !ab->fw.dualmac))
 		ab->wmi_ab.preferred_hw_mode = WMI_HOST_HW_MODE_SINGLE;
 
 	/* TODO: Init remaining wmi soc resources required */
-- 
